window.docContents[33].resolve({"/Abstraction/Function-and-program/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Function-and-program":{"contents":"A function is well typed when its types are admissible and well formed and its body is well typed, under the context of its parameters and its result type. The result type is void or storable, and a reference parameter may have an object type.\n\nA program is a list of declarations of classes and functions with a function int main(). The initial store is empty, because there are no global variables, and the result is the value of main().Two functions of one name have distinct and distinguishable signatures, . Each class  is well formed,  of . Each class template a header declares has a module of , and each function it declares has one that agrees with the declaration.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Abstraction","header":"5.5. Function and program","id":"/Abstraction/Function-and-program/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Function-and-program"}});